What is the equivalent code in Scala for constructing an if-else statement that returns "Very High" if the input number is greater than or equal to 100, "High" if it is greater than or equal to 50, "Moderate" if it is greater than or equal to 10, and "Low" otherwise? 
[Scala code]
val inputNumber = 75
if (inputNumber >= 100) {
  println("Very High")
} else if (inputNumber >= 50) {
  println("High")
} else if (inputNumber >= 10) {
  println("Moderate")
} else {
  println("Low")
}

